  "contract_findings": [
    "The dirty public server mixes the retired COD booking-advance implementation with the current no-online-payment COD route; it is not a coherent payment model.",
    "The dirty shop implementation raises the active size/colour combination limit from the retained backend limit of 20 to 100.",
    "The dirty category changes recreate a static taxonomy that was rejected in favor of the backend-authoritative store and live-catalogue contract.",
    "The dirty admin surface couples private WhatsApp links, supplier-bill storage, billing reports, GST classification, invoice issuance, commission mutation, and COD collection controls to new backend routes.",
    "Receipt and admin assets in the synchronized branch already match four pinned live targets exactly; overwriting them with the dirty versions would discard verified live lineage.",
    "Tax, invoice, supplier-bill, commission, and customer-contact features require independent Ubuntu-native implementation and security review rather than a Termux-era bulk port."
  ],
